LOCAL1="Cushion Swap cannot protect memory: no swap area is configured. What to do: name a swap file or partition as AREA= in /etc/default/cushion-swap, or give its line in /etc/fstab the noauto option, then run: sudo systemctl restart cushion-swap"
LOCAL2="Cushion Swap cannot protect memory: its swap area %s does not exist. What to do: create it, or name another area as AREA= in /etc/default/cushion-swap, then run: sudo systemctl restart cushion-swap"
LOCAL3="Cushion Swap cannot protect memory: it cannot read %s (%s), so it takes no action. It looks again every few seconds; if this stays, restart the computer."
LOCAL4="Cushion Swap cannot protect memory: it cannot read %s, so it cannot tell whether its swap area is on. It looks again every few seconds; if this stays, restart the computer."
LOCAL5="Cushion Swap could not switch its swap area on while memory runs low: swapon %s failed (%s). Memory is not protected; it tries again every few seconds. What to do: check the area with: sudo swapon %s"
LOCAL6="Cushion Swap could not switch its swap area off: swapoff %s failed (%s). The area stays on, so memory stays protected; it tries again later."
LOCAL7="The kernel's memory-stall wake-up is not available: %s. Cushion Swap checks memory every few seconds instead (compatibility mode). To repair: sudo apt-get install --reinstall sparky-stereo-cushion-swap. To make compatibility mode your choice: PSI=off in /etc/default/cushion-swap"
LOCAL8="The kernel's memory-stall wake-up does not work: %s. Cushion Swap checks memory every few seconds instead (compatibility mode). To try the wake-up again: sudo systemctl restart cushion-swap. To make compatibility mode your choice: PSI=off in /etc/default/cushion-swap"
LOCAL9="Cushion Swap could not measure how fast this computer allocates memory (%s), so it keeps the conservative pace of %s MiB/s, which samples more often and costs more CPU. It tries again a minute later, while the computer is idle. To make that pace your choice: MAX_ALLOC_MIB_S=%s in /etc/default/cushion-swap"
LOCAL10="Cushion Swap cannot measure how fast this computer allocates memory: %s. It keeps the conservative pace of %s MiB/s, which samples more often and costs more CPU. To repair: sudo apt-get install --reinstall sparky-stereo-cushion-swap. To make that pace your choice: MAX_ALLOC_MIB_S=%s in /etc/default/cushion-swap"
LOCAL11="Cushion Swap measured how fast this computer allocates memory but could not keep the result in %s (%s); it measures again at its next start."
